## [tx] The item Kits feature: staff use a craftable Kit Editor (Kit Tool) to build item bundles
## [tx] from their own inventory and configure type (Starter = auto-given on first join, Claimable =
## [tx] redeemed from a menu), name color, icon, cooldown, claim limits, rank/playtime gating,
## [tx] visibility, and pinning; regular players claim kits from the Kits section of their Player
## [tx] Tool. Strings cover form titles/fields/buttons, kit status labels, chat success/failure
## [tx] messages, two long in-game help pages, and command-automation instructions.

## [tx] Hint under an item-quantity field. %1$s = how many of this item the staff member currently
## [tx] holds in their inventory; %2$s = maximum total item count allowed across the whole kit.
jm_at.kits.amount_desc=%1$s en main, maximum total du kit : %2$s
## [tx] Text-field label asking for a quantity: %1$s = an item's display name (e.g. "Bread");
## [tx] "(whole number)" = must be an integer.
jm_at.kits.amount_label=%1$s (nombre entier)
## [tx] Help page: %1$s = the kit's name (colors stripped), %2$s = its "#id" reference. All command
## [tx] text (/scriptevent, /execute, jm_at:givekit, jm_at:claimkit, @p, @a, @initiator) must stay
## [tx] in English exactly as written — only translate the prose.
jm_at.kits.automation_body=§9§lDonner ce kit avec une commande§r\n\n§lRéférence :§r §f%1$s§r  §8(ou ID §f%2$s§8)§r\n\n§9§lDeux commandes§r\n§2§lgivekit§r — donne le kit sans tenir compte du délai ni de la limite\n§5§lclaimkit§r — récupère le kit en appliquant ses règles de délai, de limite, de grade et de temps de jeu\n\n§9§lDepuis le chat §8(opérateur)§r\nÀ vous-même :§r\n§7/scriptevent jm_at:§2givekit§r %1$s§r\nÀ un autre joueur :§r\n§7/execute as <player> run scriptevent jm_at:§2givekit§r %1$s§r\n§8P. ex. §f@p§8, §f@a§8 (tout le monde) ou un gamertag.§r\n\n§9§lDepuis un bloc de commande / PNJ§r\n§vBloc de commande :§r §f/execute as @p run scriptevent jm_at:§2givekit§r %1$s§r\n§vBouton de PNJ :§r §f/execute as @initiator run scriptevent jm_at:§2givekit§r %1$s§r\n\nRemplacez §2givekit§r par §5claimkit§r dans l’une de ces commandes pour récupérer le kit à la place. Seuls les opérateurs, ainsi que les blocs de commande et PNJ qu’ils placent, peuvent les exécuter ; les joueurs en Survie n’ont qu’à appuyer sur le bouton ou parler au PNJ.
